			"id": "agent-analysis-agent-extension-agent-card-callback-service",
			"interpretation": "Mechanism: exported class AgentExtAbility subclasses AgentExtensionAbility from @kit.AbilityKit and implements the host-facing callbacks onCreate/onConnect/onDisconnect/onData/onAuth/onDestroy, caching one common.AgentHostProxy on connect and clearing it on disconnect; onData replies via proxy.sendData and onAuth calls proxy.authorize, both try/catch-logged. Wiring: module.json5 registers an extensionAbilities entry (name AgentExtAbility, type \"agent\", exported true, srcEntry ./ets/agentextability/AgentExtAbility.ets) with metadata ohos.extension.agent pointing at $profile:agent_config; agent_config.json supplies one agentCard advertising the service's skills, modes and capabilities. build-profile.json5 pins SDK 6.1.1(24), matching README's API-24 claim, so callback signatures, profile schema and SDK pins must evolve together. Contract: keep srcEntry, type, exported flag and metadata resource name consistent with the .ets and profile; the .ets carries doc snippet markers that edits must not break; the UIAbility/Index page is only the carrier app and ohosTest merely starts EntryAbility with trivial assertions, so callback behavior has no test coverage and must be guarded by review.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["AgentExtAbility.ets casts errors with (err as BusinessError) without importing BusinessError; whether that compiles cleanly under the pinned SDK 6.1.1(24) is unproved because no compiler or hvigor build was run.","The claim that a system agent host consumes the agentCard in agent_config.json and drives onAuth/onData over AgentHostProxy is unproved: it rests on module.json5 metadata and documentation, not on device-side execution or traces.","README_zh.md points at an OpenHarmony doc URL and a sparse-checkout recipe for a different repository (applications_app_samples); their continued agreement with this checkout is unverified.","The trivial ohosTest assertions (expect(1).assertEqual(1)) cannot establish extension behavior; whether the declared test entrypoints exercise the agent callbacks at all is unproved."],
